  "raw_response": "{\n  \"title\": \"False Change of Character Trap: Bearish market lures bulls with fake breakout above supply zone before resuming downtrend\",\n  \"school\": \"Smart Money Concepts (SMC)\",\n  \"asset\": null,\n  \"timeframe\": null,\n  \"market_context\": \"Bearish market structure with prior bearish break of structure and supply zones. Price briefly rose above a supply zone, misleading novice traders into believing a reversal occurred.\",\n  \"key_observation\": \"Price broke and closed above a supply zone not to reverse trend, but to mitigate upper supply and sweep liquidity—creating a false CHoCH that trapped longs.\",\n  \"analysis_steps\": [\n    \"Step 1: Analyst identified a bearish market structure with prior bearish BOS and associated supply zones.\",\n    \"Step 2: Noted price moved up and broke/closed above the last supply zone, which novices misinterpreted as a valid CHoCH.\",\n    \"Step 3: Clarified the upward move was not from an unmitigated demand zone but served to mitigate upper supply and act as inducement.\",\n    \"Step 4: Explained that price used the supply zone as a breaker block to sweep liquidity (stop-losses of longs) before continuing downward.\"\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": null,\n  \"lessons\": \"A valid CHoCH requires price to reverse from an unmitigated demand zone—not a supply zone used as inducement. False breakouts above supply often precede liquidity sweeps and trend continuation.\",\n  \"primary_image_frame_id\": \"sxaR_PjEcuM_f011\",\n  \"supporting_image_frame_ids\": [],\n  \"related_concepts\": [\"Chang",
